3d-anatomy (MEDCOEL Anatomy Atlas) - licence of the work as distributed
=======================================================================

STATUS: LICENCE QUARANTINE IN EFFECT SINCE 2026-11-09
-----------------------------------------------------

An audit found components whose redistribution rights could not be verified,
or whose terms conflict with the ShareAlike licence of the rest of the work.
Those components are WITHHELD from this distribution until they are cleared in
writing. The machine-readable policy is licensing/quarantine-policy.json in the
MEDCOEL monorepo; the full report is licensing/PROVENANCE_REPORT.md.

Withheld (not present in public/ or in any build, in any form):

  * public/models/nervous.glb, entirely. It contained:
      - "Brainder" and "White matter" (University of Washington) brain meshes,
        for which the upstream notice states NO licence;
      - "Anatomy of the Inner Ear" (University of Dundee, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0,
        itself a derivative of McGill "3D Ear", CC BY-NC-SA 1.0);
      - other brain, brainstem, cerebellar, nerve and sense-organ meshes whose
        individual origin could not be separated from the above with confidence.
  * The kidney model "Kidney - by lissiecowley - CC-BY-NC 4.0" (Kidney.l,
    Kidney.r) and the renal pelvis (Renal pelvis.l, Renal pelvis.r), removed
    from public/models/visceral.glb.
  * The auditory ossicles (Malleus, Incus, Stapes, both sides), removed from
    public/models/skeletal.glb as a precaution: the upstream inner-ear model
    (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) states that it includes the ossicles.
  * Every preview image rendered from the withheld meshes.

The viewer shows withheld anatomy as "tidak tersedia" (unavailable). It does not
substitute other or fabricated models.


SUMMARY OF THE TERMS NOW IN EFFECT
----------------------------------

1. Anatomical models (public/models/*.glb) and previews (public/thumbnails/)

   Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

   After the quarantine, every remaining mesh is attributed upstream to
   BodyParts3D (CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan) as reworked by Z-Anatomy (CC BY-SA 4.0).
   CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan allows adaptations to be licensed under a later version
   of the licence with the same elements, so CC BY-SA 4.0 is used for the
   whole set. skeletal.glb and visceral.glb are MEDCOEL adaptations: nodes were
   removed losslessly (all other geometry is byte-identical) and each file
   carries an embedded modification notice (asset.extras).

   ATTRIBUTION is required; the strings are in NOTICE. SHARE-ALIKE: adaptations
   must be distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0 or a compatible licence.

2. Definitions of the anatomical structures (public/data/definitions.json)

   Wikipedia contributors, CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL, with very few modifications.
   https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Copyrights

3. Application source code (index.html, src/, public/styles/, tools/, build
   configuration)

   Unchanged by the quarantine: the original author released it under
   CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 to keep one set of conditions for the bundle. That choice no
   longer follows from the models (they are now BY-SA only) and is for the
   project owner to revisit. Creative Commons does not recommend its licences
   for software.

Blender was used to produce the exported models. Its own licence is included
in the upstream 'Anatomy Blender' distribution and is not reproduced here.


COLLECTION VERSUS ADAPTATION
----------------------------

Each .glb file is a single adaptation of the upstream Z-Anatomy export (meshes
from several upstream works merged into one scene graph and one binary). Files
served side by side by the viewer form a collection. Derived products that
fuse geometry from several meshes into new data (for example the 4D Lab's
voxelised CT, label map and skin shell) are adaptations of every mesh that
contributed. A NonCommercial component cannot be fused into a ShareAlike
adaptation and still satisfy both licences; this is why the kidney was removed
rather than relabelled.


